---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import HomeHero from '../components/HomeHero.astro';
import {articles,sections,sectionDescriptions,tours,url} from '../lib/content';
const milestones=[['E17','Original-client pixels','A known pattern, then the setup graphic on the real panel.'],['E20','Physical button wake','A Power tap reaches original HID and restores the image.'],['E13','Checked storage + reboot','Two consecutive bounded boots; complete data checks pass.'],['E23','Measured charging','A controlled 12-minute trial: 29% → 31% battery.']];
---
<Base>
<HomeHero/>
<section class="scope-strip"><span class="mono">THE STUDY</span><p>Original iPhone OS userspace. Adapted XNU. An A64 PinePhone. <br/><span>A preserved reference in emulation, and a native port examined one boundary at a time.</span></p><a href={url('articles/three-machines/')}>Understand the three environments ↗</a></section>
<section class="home-section discoveries"><div class="section-intro"><span class="section-number">01 — FINDINGS</span><h2>What the experiments <br/>actually establish.</h2><p>Four physical milestones. Each has a method, an observation and a limit.</p><a class="text-link" href={url('evidence/')}>Open the evidence ledger →</a></div><div class="finding-list">{milestones.map(([id,title,desc])=><a class="finding" href={url('evidence/'+id+'/')}><span class="evidence-id">{id}<i class="line"/></span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{desc}</p></div><span class="arrow">↗</span></a>)}<p class="limits-note"><strong>THE PUBLISHED BOUNDARY</strong>These records establish a setup display with button interaction. Later development observations—including touch and camera—are tracked separately in the <a href="/ios/status/">capability status →</a></p></div></section>
<section class="home-section chapter-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-number">02 — THE ATLAS</span><h2>Read the system in layers.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={url('library/')}>All {articles.length} chapters →</a></div><div class="domain-list">{sections.map((section,i)=><a href={url('library/#'+section.toLowerCase())} class="domain-row" data-domain={section}><span class="domain-no">{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h3>{section}</h3><p>{sectionDescriptions[section]}</p><span class="domain-count">{articles.filter(a=>a.section===section).length} chapters <span>↗</span></span></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="home-section tours-section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="section-number">03 — READING PATHS</span><h2>Choose a way in.</h2></div><p>Guided sequences through connected ideas.</p></div><div class="tour-grid">{tours.map((tour,i)=><a class="tour" href={url('tours/'+tour.id+'/')}><span class="tour-index">PATH {String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}<span>{tour.slugs.length} stops</span></span><svg viewBox="0 0 290 80" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 40H282" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.3"/>{tour.slugs.map((_,n)=><circle cx={8+n*274/(tour.slugs.length-1)} cy="40" r={n===0?4.5:3} fill={n===0?'currentColor':'var(--surface)'} stroke="currentColor"/>)}</svg><h3>{tour.title}</h3><p>{tour.description}</p><span class="text-link">Follow this path →</span></a>)}</div></section>
<section class="correction-feature"><span class="section-number">RESEARCH IS ALSO REVISION</span><h2>The useful discoveries <br/>included being wrong.</h2><div><p>A zero-filled buffer was an ineffective probe. A missing console message was an unreliable milestone. A radio detected by the emulator did not exist.</p><a class="button light" href={url('method/#corrections')}>Read the correction ledger <span>↗</span></a></div></section>
</Base>